          ],
          "ontology_mapping.evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
              "source": "CultureMech",
              "notes": "Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH"
            },
            {
              "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
              "source": "MIM curation (#319/#320)",
              "notes": "identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:64755 ('EDTA(2-)') -> CHEBI:4735 ('ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid'); mapping_quality -> SYNONYM_MATCH. ChEBI's live definition of CHEBI:64755 is 'a tetracarboxylic acid anion formed by deprotonation of TWO of the four carboxy groups' — a specific charge state this record's label never asserts. Under #319's rule a specific definition means descend, unlike the 'at least one' wording that keeps the anion. Absorbed 'EDTA (acid form)', which held the free-acid term with ZERO occurrences and already carried 'EDTA' as a synonym. The corpus keeps separate Na2-EDTA records for the salt, so plain 'EDTA' denoting the free acid is consistent with how the rest of the family is modelled."
            }
          ]
        },
        "interpretation": "These exact source/preparation/role/occurrence restrictions remain; changing a mapping assertion or rejecting a label does not approve the unresolved material or source claims."
